but in the mechanics as well.

123
00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:54.960
The processor makes you work together
to share resources and lean on each other

124
00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.120
in intimate ways.

125
00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.800
It's not just about shared space,

126
00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.800
but about shared materiality
and shared constraints.

127
00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:01.960
Our goal is to create

128
00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:06.400
an embodied experience of what it means
to lose out on choices that matter to you.

129
00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.000
As stated by Piercey and Virga,

130
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:14.320
utilizing experiential play allows us
to examine what Brandon Quixote calls

131
00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:17.320
