136
00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:32.400
and asymmetrical narrative knowledge
between players and electronic literature.

137
00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:37.080
Nodding to Sarah Ahmed, we reflect on
how bodies as well as objects, take shape

138
00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:41.560
through being oriented toward each other
as an orientation that may be experienced

139
00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:45.640
as the cohabitation of sharing space
or sharing of space.

140
00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.640
As such, the queer narratives in ether
five push what it means

141
00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:52.000
to be queer with more
than just the POV of one character.

142
00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:56.120
We ask, what does it mean
to experience a queer narrative together?

143
00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:58.800
Now, as

144
00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:01.800
we're exploring the answers
to some of these recurring questions,

145
00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:05.320
one of the more immediate questions
we were asking was,

146
00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:08.720
can we build a toolkit,
an ecosystem of tools where the barriers

147
00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:12.840
to implementing copious
where are modularized and supported.

148
00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.080
And Godot became our engine of choice
for several reasons.

149
00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:19.920
It has a strong willed, documented
UI library, which makes it well suited

150
00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:24.240
