156
00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.120
So how do we write this game together
efficiently?

157
00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.480
Our initial approach was a custom
dialog manager designed to power

158
00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:45.760
stacks from a JSON file
with right side by side in a CSV

159
00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.320
tagging passages and choices
from a predefined set of options.

160
00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.920
And our pipeline
would convert the CSV to JSON

161
00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:55.320
and have our dialog manager parse
and render the text and choices

162
00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:59.080
and their relationships in each player's
respective panels.

163
00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:01.560
But while this works
for very simple mechanics,

164
00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:06.080
